    "lessons": [
      {
        "id": "oxford-1-1",
        "title": "A surprising airport visit",
        "subtitle": "旅行与偶遇",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "en": "This afternoon, I arrive at the airport with a friend. We look at the screen above the desk and ask about our flight. The answer is good: we have time for tea. My friend checks the address of our hotel again.",
            "zh": "今天下午（afternoon），我和一位（a）朋友来到机场（airport）。我们看着柜台上方（above）的屏幕，并且（and）询问关于（about）航班的情况。答复（answer）不错：我们还有时间喝茶。朋友再次（again）核对酒店的地址（address）。",
            "patterns": [
              {
                "expression": "arrive at the airport",
                "meaning": "到达机场；arrive at 后接具体地点"
              },
              {
                "expression": "have time for tea",
                "meaning": "有时间喝茶；have time for 后接名词"
              },
              {
                "expression": "ask about our flight",
                "meaning": "询问航班情况"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "en": "Across the room, an actor and an actress are talking to children. I saw their amazing film a week ago. They also give advice to a young fan: always be kind. After a photo, all the children smile, and we agree that this is a lovely start to our trip.",
            "zh": "在房间对面（across），一名演员（actor）和（and）一名女演员（actress）正与孩子们交谈。我在一（a）周以前（ago）看过他们那部令人惊叹的（amazing）电影。他们也（also）给年轻影迷提建议（advice）：总是（always）要友善。合影之后（after），所有（all）孩子都笑了，我们一致认为（agree），这趟旅程有了美好的开端。",
            "patterns": [
              {
                "expression": "give advice to a young fan",
                "meaning": "给一位年轻影迷提建议；advice 为不可数名词"
              },
              {
                "expression": "a week ago",
                "meaning": "一周前；时间长度 + ago 表示距今多久以前"
              },
              {
                "expression": "agree that this is a lovely start",
                "meaning": "一致认为这是美好的开端；agree that 后接完整句子"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "questions": [
          {
            "word": "actor",
            "prompt": "In \"an actor\", what does \"actor\" mean?",
            "options": [
              "a person who checks flight tickets",
              "a person who cares for animals",
              "a person who performs in plays or films",
              "a person who cooks meals"
            ],
            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": "actor 指在戏剧或电影里表演的人。短文随后提到他们的电影，帮助你判断这是演员，而不是机场工作人员。actor 可以指任何性别的演员。"
          },
          {
            "word": "actress",
            "prompt": "In \"an actress\", what does \"actress\" mean?",
            "options": [
              "a woman who writes addresses",
              "a woman who flies planes",
              "a woman who grows vegetables",
              "a woman who performs in plays or films"
            ],
            "answer": 3,
            "explanation": "actress 专指女演员。它与短文中的 film 和 actor 属于同一主题，不能理解为女飞行员或园丁。"
          },
          {
            "word": "airport",
            "prompt": "In \"at the airport\", what does \"airport\" mean?",
            "options": [
              "a place where planes arrive and leave",
              "a place where books are borrowed",
              "a place where films are made",
              "a place where meals are cooked"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": "airport 是飞机起降、旅客乘坐航班的地方。短文的 flight 和 screen 提供了机场情境的线索。"
          },
          {
            "word": "address",
            "prompt": "In \"the address of our hotel\", what does \"address\" mean?",
            "options": [
              "the cost of a meal",
              "details of where someone lives or stays",
              "the time a flight leaves",
              "the name of an animal"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": "address 在这里是名词“地址”，告诉我们酒店在哪里。航班时间和费用都不能用来说明酒店的具体位置。"
          },
          {
            "word": "ago",
            "prompt": "In \"a week ago\", what does \"ago\" mean?",
            "options": [
              "from now on",
              "before now",
              "at the present moment",
              "once more"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": "ago 与表示时间长度的词组一起使用，表示距现在多久以前。a week ago 是“一周前”，不是“一周后”。"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "oxford-1-2",
        "title": "A small stage, a big moment",
        "subtitle": "戏剧与勇气",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "en": "Our drama group meets every afternoon. One actor is my age, but the actress playing his mother is an adult. Today, our first activity is a short scene about a lost bag. There is plenty of action: we run across the stage and search under chairs.",
            "zh": "我们剧团每天下午（afternoon）见面。一名演员（actor）和我年龄（age）相同，但扮演他母亲的女演员（actress）是一名成年人（adult）。今天的第一个活动（activity）是一（a）段关于（about）丢包的短戏。戏里有很多动作（action）：我们跑过（across）舞台，并且（and）到椅子下面寻找。",
            "patterns": [
              {
                "expression": "my age",
                "meaning": "与我同龄；be my age 表示年龄与我相同"
              },
              {
                "expression": "plenty of action",
                "meaning": "很多动作；plenty of 可接不可数名词"
              },
              {
                "expression": "search under chairs",
                "meaning": "在椅子下面寻找"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "en": "I am afraid of forgetting my words. Our teacher is never angry when we make mistakes. She gives us another chance and says, \"Take a breath and try again.\" We all agree to help each other. After the show, I feel amazing.",
            "zh": "我害怕（afraid）忘词。我们犯错时，老师从不生气（angry）。她再给我们一次（another）机会，并且（and）说：“吸一（a）口气，再次（again）尝试。”我们所有人（all）都同意（agree）互相帮助。演出之后（after），我感觉棒极了（amazing）。",
            "patterns": [
              {
                "expression": "afraid of forgetting my words",
                "meaning": "害怕忘词；be afraid of 后接名词或动词 -ing 形式"
              },
              {
                "expression": "make mistakes",
                "meaning": "犯错"
              },
              {
                "expression": "agree to help each other",
                "meaning": "同意互相帮助；agree to 后接动词原形"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "questions": [
          {
            "word": "activity",
            "prompt": "In \"our first activity\", what does \"activity\" mean?",
            "options": [
              "a number showing age",
              "something people do",
              "a person in a film",
              "the air outside"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": "activity 指安排大家做的一项活动。这里具体是排演一段丢包的短戏；它不是人的年龄或身份。"
          },
          {
            "word": "afraid",
            "prompt": "In \"afraid of forgetting my words\", what does \"afraid\" mean?",
            "options": [
              "feeling fear",
              "feeling hunger",
              "feeling pride",
              "feeling boredom"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": "afraid 表示害怕、担心。人物担心忘掉台词，所以它不是“饥饿”或“自豪”；afraid of 后可接动词 -ing 形式。"
          },
          {
            "word": "angry",
            "prompt": "In \"never angry\", what does \"angry\" mean?",
            "options": [
              "feeling very sleepy",
              "feeling completely calm",
              "feeling strong displeasure",
              "feeling very curious"
            ],
            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": "angry 表示生气、不高兴。never angry 说明老师不会因学生犯错而生气；angry 本身并不表示“平静”。"
          },
          {
            "word": "again",
            "prompt": "In \"try again\", what does \"again\" mean?",
            "options": [
              "for the first time",
              "at no time",
              "at the same place",
              "one more time"
